Track 1: Telescope Lenses Melting in the Parades
- Story & Context: On the tin roofs of Barrio Corona, sixteen-year-old brass prodigy Valeria wired her father's heirloom marching tuba directly into an open-source granular synthesizer just as the shadow of the moon hit the coast. The sudden surge of static blew the city’s power grid, but her battery-powered rig screamed out an ungodly, shuffling bassline that brought the panicked street crowds into a unified, euphoric dance. As solar flare flares flickered across the blackout, she leaned into the microphone and shouted, "The sun is gone so we burn the copper!" The track instantly circulated via peer-to-peer bluetooth networks, marking the birth of Umbrafall.
