- Story & Context: As the three-minute eclipse drew to a close over the city, the Syndicate recorded the final reverb tail of their set decaying into the returning afternoon heat. This track acts as the haunting aftermath, blending stretched out gaita flutes with a slow-burning synth bass that feels like walking through hot asphalt after a storm. Legend says the final synth drop was recorded by pointing a microphone directly at a melting telescope lens that caught fire under the focused sun. The track closes with a whispered vocal hook, "Cover your eyes, daylight is coming back to ruin the magic."
